Keeping up with Alix Earle is beyond the capacity of most mere mortals. Over the past year alone, Earle could be found delivering a perfect foxtrot on Dancing With the Stars weeks before shimmying alongside Pedro Pascal and Cardi B on Bad Bunny's Super Bowl Halftime Show; vibing to Lady Gaga's Coachella set and hours later lecturing a Harvard Business School class about the creator economy; falling in sky-high platforms at Kendall Jenner's L.A. Halloween party, then strolling New York's CFDA Awards red carpet (bruises hidden) in a gown styled by Law Roach. For weeks this summer, she cruised in a yacht along the Sardinia coast with Kylie Jenner BFF Stassie Karanikolaou, flying to Los Angeles for the Sept. 1 premiere of her Netflix reality series Earle Meets World (a global top 10 debut just renewed for a second season), all while weathering headlines about a rumored fling with Tom Brady and the messy fallout of a business rift with Call Her Daddy &#8216;s Alex Cooper. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Lifestyle Oprah's Favorite Things 30th Anniversary List Includes Actor-Owned Apparel, Celeb-Approved Skin Care and More Lifestyle The 5 Best Red Light Therapy Panels for Improving Your Health At-Home

The quickest way to locate this 25-year-old jet-set influencer is, of course, on TikTok , where her videos have attracted 8.7 million followers, with each post garnering view counts in the millions (not to mention 1.7 billion likes) for documenting all of the above in real time. Her meteoric rise on social media kicked off during the pandemic, filming &#8220;get ready with me&#8221; makeup tutorials in between marketing classes, wild party nights, battles with anxiety and a breast-implant &#8220;boobaversary,&#8221; while she attended the University of Miami. She reads as a sorority girl, but IRL, her vibe is more tough-cookie-from-a-Jersey-construction-family who exudes the kind of warmth that might have you bellied to the bar, sipping margs and having a kiki. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

At the moment, though, seated in a sunny conference room inside Reale Actives' Beverly Hills office, she's taking her magnetic energy and putting it to work on keeping her winning streak alive.

Less than eight months ago, on March 31, Earle launched Reale Actives, a skin care brand formulated in collaboration with dermatologist Kiran Mian and tailored for sensitive and acne-prone skin. Developed in secret for two years, the four-product launch drew a record-breaking response from Earle's online community &#x2014; a fiercely supportive tribe, particularly after she shared a years-long, psychologically debilitating struggle with cystic acne. It generated $1 million in sales in less than five minutes. By midday, sales hit $5 million, and by 4 p.m., all products and sets had sold out completely.

It's nearly lunchtime on a late-October day, and Earle, at the head of the table, is introducing five members of her team: CEO Andrea Blieden, director of influencer marketing and partnerships Katie Clementi, brand director Brianna Ellis-Mitchell, social director Logan Reynolds and, on Zoom, chief marketing officer Amanda Goetz. By year's end, there will be 23 full-time employees across two office floors.

