How did Killer Films end up boarding In Starland ? &#8220;We asked Christine if she'd take a look and read the script and watch what we shot,&#8221; Panthaki says. &#8220;We had a conversation with her and over many conversations she just believed in the project. For me, that someone of that clout and and someone who has that amazing body of work believed in it is the biggest seal of approval. I'm so grateful to her and to Mason Plotts [, head of film at Killer Films].&#8221;

Audience will recognize 1980s music throughout In Starland . Given his own love for it, Panthaki says that he simply had to make one of his young characters be obsessed with music from that period. One of the key tunes in the film is the Tears for Fears hit &#8220;Everybody Wants to Rule the World.&#8221;

