Asked about the film's title, Panthaki tells THR : &#8220;I wanted something that felt poetic and really explained what the film was in a number of ways, and it just came to me. In Starland was a play on words because if you put those words together, it almost sounds like Instaland, so it has the Instagram element, and Ernie was in starland &#x2013;&#xA0;but I don't want to talk about a key twist there. I wanted to have a duality in the title, much like the lives of the people in the film.&#8221;

Could we see another feature directed by Panthaki? &#8220;Writing, directing and producing this film has been the hardest thing I've ever done in my life,&#8221; he shares. &#8220;Everything that has happened in this movie over the past seven years has been 10 times harder because we were doing it ourselves. So, will I do it again? I think yes. But I don't know if I can do it again with so little time and money. I think I'll need more infrastructure in place to be able to do it again.&#8221;

That said, Panthaki's passion is coming through again. &#8220;I have ideas that are burning in me, and it has to be something I want to say about the world,&#8221; he tells THR . &#8220;It has to be something important that I can say, and something that I can do well. So I've got a couple of ideas that I'm working on. But for right now, get me back to acting!&#8221;

